WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.463 --> 00:00:01.732
- Good morning, Believe Nation!

00:00:01.732 --> 00:00:02.759
My name is Evan Carmichael.

00:00:02.759 --> 00:00:05.213
My one word is believe, and
I believe that entrepreneurs

00:00:05.213 --> 00:00:07.594
will solve all of the world's problems.

00:00:07.594 --> 00:00:10.953
Today's message is Don't
Care What Others Think.

00:00:10.953 --> 00:00:12.796
Over to you Warren Buffett.

00:00:12.796 --> 00:00:15.278
(rooster crowing)

00:00:15.278 --> 00:00:17.750
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:20.547
♫ Espresso keep me goin'

00:00:20.547 --> 00:00:24.481
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:24.481 --> 00:00:27.503
- It never bothered me if people disagreed

00:00:27.503 --> 00:00:31.180
with what I thought as long
as I felt I knew the facts.

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:32.889
I mean, there's a whole bunch of things

00:00:32.889 --> 00:00:33.918
I don't know a thing about (laughs).

00:00:33.918 --> 00:00:35.033
I just stay away from those.

00:00:35.033 --> 00:00:39.200
So I stay within what I call
my circle of competency,

00:00:40.072 --> 00:00:41.221
and Tom Watson said it best.

00:00:41.221 --> 00:00:44.288
He said, "I'm no genius,
but I'm smart in spots,

00:00:44.288 --> 00:00:45.600
"and I stay around those spots."

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:47.428
Well, I try and stay around those spots

00:00:47.428 --> 00:00:51.511
and I just don't have a
problem if somebody says,

00:00:52.442 --> 00:00:53.889
"You're wrong on something."

00:00:53.889 --> 00:00:55.784
I just go back and look at the facts

00:00:55.784 --> 00:00:59.951
and I think that really is
much more important, frankly,

00:01:01.195 --> 00:01:03.622
than having a few points of IQ,

00:01:03.622 --> 00:01:06.315
or having an extra
course or two in school,

00:01:06.315 --> 00:01:07.148
or anything of the sort.

00:01:07.148 --> 00:01:09.122
You need emotional stability.

00:01:09.122 --> 00:01:10.527
- I really love that last bit

00:01:10.527 --> 00:01:12.774
that he talked about, emotional stability.

00:01:12.774 --> 00:01:14.628
I think it's really
important for entrepreneurs

00:01:14.628 --> 00:01:18.166
to understand where your
threshold is of how much

00:01:18.166 --> 00:01:20.496
crap you can take from other people,

00:01:20.496 --> 00:01:23.703
how much negativity, how
much feedback and criticism

00:01:23.703 --> 00:01:26.471
that you can take without
it impacting your psyche

00:01:26.471 --> 00:01:27.950
or your self-worth.

00:01:27.950 --> 00:01:29.323
I think, in general, as an entrepreneur

00:01:29.323 --> 00:01:31.962
you need to be prepared
to get a lot of crap,

00:01:31.962 --> 00:01:34.439
a lot of negativity, a lot
of stuff thrown at you,

00:01:34.439 --> 00:01:36.031
and yes, it's easy to say,

00:01:36.031 --> 00:01:37.403
don't care what other people think,

00:01:37.403 --> 00:01:40.805
but understanding what
your tolerance level is,

00:01:40.805 --> 00:01:43.086
and where you kind of
fit on that spectrum,

00:01:43.086 --> 00:01:45.520
can really help you design the rules,

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:46.919
so that they're in your favor.

00:01:46.919 --> 00:01:49.257
So as an example, there's a guy on my team

00:01:49.257 --> 00:01:52.366
who doesn't handle criticism as well.

00:01:52.366 --> 00:01:55.285
I'm a lot more comfortable
in the uncomfortable,

00:01:55.285 --> 00:01:57.857
where he can bounce around a lot more.

00:01:57.857 --> 00:02:00.070
He'll be on top of the
world, like this is great,

00:02:00.070 --> 00:02:02.869
and then a negative feedback
comes in and it really impacts

00:02:02.869 --> 00:02:05.232
him hardly, and then a
positive one comes in

00:02:05.232 --> 00:02:07.997
and he jumps back up, and
so for someone like him,

00:02:07.997 --> 00:02:11.304
you can't design as much
risk, as much negativity

00:02:11.304 --> 00:02:15.471
or potential negativity so you
got to take a safe path up.

00:02:16.317 --> 00:02:19.458
Where for me, I'm more
comfortable in the uncomfortable.

00:02:19.458 --> 00:02:22.193
I know that eventually
something's going to work out,

00:02:22.193 --> 00:02:24.312
and I know that at the
beginning of any project,

00:02:24.312 --> 00:02:27.811
it's going to be rough,
that it may not work out,

00:02:27.811 --> 00:02:29.614
that we're going to get some criticism,

00:02:29.614 --> 00:02:32.619
and so I'm more willing to jump all in,

00:02:32.619 --> 00:02:34.913
in playing that field,
even though it's painful

00:02:34.913 --> 00:02:37.168
at the moment because I know
the faster I get through

00:02:37.168 --> 00:02:39.383
that pain, the faster I'm going
to come out the other side.

00:02:39.383 --> 00:02:42.007
I want that feedback,
and criticism negativity

00:02:42.007 --> 00:02:45.038
as soon as possible, so
that I can make it better!

00:02:45.038 --> 00:02:47.680
Better for you, better for
me, better for everybody!

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:51.133
And so understanding what
your tolerance level is,

00:02:51.133 --> 00:02:54.070
of emotional stability,
how much you can take,

00:02:54.070 --> 00:02:55.743
from your friends and your family

00:02:55.743 --> 00:02:57.388
and your customers and your
audience and the people

00:02:57.388 --> 00:03:00.352
watching you, before your
break, and then being able

00:03:00.352 --> 00:03:02.179
to play, just below that limit.

00:03:02.179 --> 00:03:04.108
'Cause you can't just play super-safe,

00:03:04.108 --> 00:03:06.149
'cause that's not going to make
you happy as an entrepreneur.

00:03:06.149 --> 00:03:08.856
But know what your limit is
and playing just below it,

00:03:08.856 --> 00:03:11.042
so that it's uncomfortable, it's painful,

00:03:11.042 --> 00:03:12.732
but your still going to
be able to get through it,

00:03:12.732 --> 00:03:15.124
I think is really important,
that self-awareness,

00:03:15.124 --> 00:03:16.857
I think is really important
as an entrepreneur.

00:03:16.857 --> 00:03:19.100
So the question today is, I'm curious,

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:22.702
how high is your tolerance
level for taking criticism

00:03:22.702 --> 00:03:24.058
from other people?

00:03:24.058 --> 00:03:25.384
How much does it bother you

00:03:25.384 --> 00:03:27.417
and can you get through it or not?

00:03:27.417 --> 00:03:28.594
Really curious to find out.

00:03:28.594 --> 00:03:30.175
Please leave it down
in the comments below.

00:03:30.175 --> 00:03:32.593
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Leithland Lyon.

00:03:32.593 --> 00:03:34.164
Leithland, thank you so
much for picking up a copy

00:03:34.164 --> 00:03:36.167
of my book, Your One Word.

00:03:36.167 --> 00:03:37.668
I really, really, appreciate the support,

00:03:37.668 --> 00:03:39.796
and I hope you're enjoying the read.

00:03:39.796 --> 00:03:41.195
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:03:41.195 --> 00:03:42.385
I believe in you.

00:03:42.385 --> 00:03:44.311
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself,

00:03:44.311 --> 00:03:46.504
and whatever your one word is,

00:03:46.504 --> 00:03:47.930
and I'll see you again tomorrow morning

00:03:47.930 --> 00:03:50.686
for another shot of Entspresso!

00:03:50.686 --> 00:03:53.226
♫ I wake up every morning

00:03:53.226 --> 00:03:56.929
♫ Espresso keep me goin'

00:03:56.929 --> 00:03:59.929
(keyboard clicking)

00:05:04.737 --> 00:05:07.143
- How did you ignore all
those naysayers and continue

00:05:07.143 --> 00:05:08.473
to sort of blaze the trail --

00:05:08.473 --> 00:05:12.853
- Well 95 percent of
all new ventures fail,

00:05:12.853 --> 00:05:15.555
so if you just bet
against all new ventures,

00:05:15.555 --> 00:05:18.130
odds are 90 percent that
you're going to be right,

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:20.153
90 percent of the time,

00:05:20.153 --> 00:05:23.548
but, you're going to
miss that one out of ten

00:05:23.548 --> 00:05:27.715
or one out of 20 chances
to really hit a home run.

00:05:28.594 --> 00:05:32.990
And, I wasn't worried
about the naysayers saying

00:05:32.990 --> 00:05:33.978
it wasn't going to work.

00:05:33.978 --> 00:05:38.049
I just laughed about it,
because I knew it was.

00:05:38.049 --> 00:05:39.333
- And you worked very hard at it as well.

00:05:39.333 --> 00:05:41.840
- I wasn't going to let it fail.

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:44.553
And if you read my book, it's right there.

00:05:44.553 --> 00:05:46.803
I wasn't going to let it fail,

00:05:48.078 --> 00:05:50.481
and I'm not going to let,

00:05:50.481 --> 00:05:51.770
I'm not going to let humanity fail

00:05:51.770 --> 00:05:53.148
to get rid of nuclear weapons

00:05:53.148 --> 00:05:55.565
and handle this energy thing.

00:05:56.896 --> 00:06:00.254
I'm going to keep fighting
till we start getting it right.

00:06:00.254 --> 00:06:01.795
- [Interviewer] Pay a lot
of attention to reviews

00:06:01.795 --> 00:06:03.018
and those kind of things.

00:06:03.018 --> 00:06:05.974
- Well, you know, you're
always affected by opinion,

00:06:05.974 --> 00:06:09.224
but the more opinions there are of you,

00:06:10.174 --> 00:06:13.591
of me, the more, the less I look at them,

00:06:15.011 --> 00:06:16.431
because I just can't live my life

00:06:16.431 --> 00:06:19.055
based upon what other
people think about me.

00:06:19.055 --> 00:06:20.723
So I can't concern myself too much with

00:06:20.723 --> 00:06:23.747
what other people think, you
know, it's just not healthy.

00:06:23.747 --> 00:06:26.014
I don't think I could continue to do what

00:06:26.014 --> 00:06:27.954
I do if I was constantly worrying about

00:06:27.954 --> 00:06:29.162
what somebody thought about it.

